at least either of the two elemental states x_{1}-{0} or x_{1}-{P} are active in the initial state, both will be active in the attractor. Both elemental states need to be inactive in the initial state to be absent (inactive) in the attractor state. Both reaction nodes r_{1} and r_{2} are assumed to be active in this example and are not shown. Synthesis and degradation are not considered here. In the example, standard update rules are applied, where two mutually exclusive states can be simultaneously present. More details can be found in [29].","figureTypeId":"multipanel","panels":[{"panel":"A","typeId":"network"},{"panel":"B","typeId":"state_transition"},{"panel":"C","typeId":"mechanism"}],"match":{"level":"exact","score":1010,"requestedTypeId":"state_transition","preferences":{},"reason":"图型或明确标注的子图精确匹配"},"layout":"grid","density":"high","designLessons":["同一布尔网络分别呈现实体连接、全状态转移、反应机制及真值表，展示节点语义随图型改变。"],"doNotTransfer":["A节点是变量，B节点是整组布尔状态，C含反应节点，不能互相混用。D是表格，不能为了填补覆盖而标成二值矩阵图。","原论文的实体名称、样本、数值、显著性、模型性能与科学结论。"],"attribution":"Ulrike Münzner, Tomoya Mori, Marcus Krantz, Edda Klipp, Tatsuya Akutsu. Identification of periodic attractors in Boolean networks using a priori information. PLOS Computational Biology (2022), Fig 1. 10.1371/journal.pcbi.1009702. CC-BY-4.0.","license":"CC-BY-4.0"}]","topology":{"schemaVersion":1,"nodes":[{"id":"n_30fd62d4883253d0","label":"Idle","shape":"process","role":"normal"},{"id":"n_ea77288f6e0587f2","label":"Running","shape":"process","role":"normal"},{"id":"n_96722239eb13e2fa","label":"Paused","shape":"process","role":"normal"},{"id":"n_5959f4734ee67303","label":"Completed","shape":"process","role":"normal"},{"id":"n_9816b44bae2956de","label":"","shape":"initial","role":"initial","initialEvidence":{"sourceQuote":"Initial dot enters Idle.","markerQuote":"Initial dot enters Idle.","interpretation":"explicit_unnamed_initial"}}],"edges":[{"id":"edge_0","source":"n_9816b44bae2956de","target":"n_30fd62d4883253d0","label":"","sourceQuote":"Initial d